---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Robert Potts — Editing" active="editing">
  <div class="page editing">
    <PageHeader title="Editing" />

    <div class="editing__body">
      <p class="placeholder-note">
        Placeholder text — Robert will write about his editing work here.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside criticism, I work as an editor: with poets and prose writers, with
        magazines, and occasionally with book-length manuscripts that have lost their way.
        This page is where I will describe that work — the kinds of projects I take on, how I
        like to work with a writer, and a few of the things I have helped bring into print.
      </p>
      <p>
        Good editing is mostly listening. The aim is never to make a piece sound like me, but
        to help it sound more fully like itself — to find the argument beneath the draft and
        clear away whatever is standing in its light. Sometimes that means deep structural
        work; sometimes it is a matter of a dozen small cuts.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you would like to talk about an editing project, the best place to reach me is via
        the links on the <a href="/">About</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .editing {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  .editing__body {
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .placeholder-note {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
</style>
